    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **53 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe membership-level rule lives in `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel(...)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`).\n\nPreviously it computed `1 + email + namesake0` and then did an unconditional `Math.min(level, 3)`. That accidentally satisfied the new test but didn't express the spec \u2014 level 4 was simply unreachable for everyone, rather than being a tenure-gated tier.\n\nNow the method:\n1. Computes the pre-tenure factors (`1` base, `+1` for an email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`) and caps that portion at 3.\n2. Adds the level-4 loyalty tier **only** when tenure \u2014 days from `registrationDate` to the current date \u2014 is **more than 365 days**.\n\nBecause a newly created owner is registered on the current date, its tenure is zero, so it can never reach level 4. The example from the spec (email + `namesakeCount` 0 + 3-member household) lands at level 3, which the new `Cp39Tests` asserts, while the existing membership tests (`Cp15`, `Cp23`, `Cp24`) remain unchanged since they all create fresh, zero-tenure owners.",
